			<div class="content" id="post-content-1849977">
									

<p>The warm glow of your approval has inspired me to complete the set.</p>
<p>-14 and 15 never really got along. Sibling rivalry between twin sisters can be a blood sport But that didn't matter to the man the papers dubbed &quot;The Surgeon&quot;. All he cared about was their <em>physical</em> compatibility. The police raid on his cabin only found one survivor. Many papers were published based on forensic examination of the hundreds of grafts and transplants that he inflicted on her, some of which should have been medically impossible to survive. Nearly as many psychological papers have been published regarding her PTSD, survivor's guilt, and DID. The shrinks said it was perfectly normal for her to manifest delusions, believing that she was actually her sister was just the psyche's way of processing the trauma. Their explanations sounded a bit forced when new, fully-formed and impossibly self-consistent personalities emerged; seemingly a new one every day. They had nothing at all to say when the records and valid birth certificates for each of them.</p>
<p>-19 was not adjusting well to her new situation. She wasn't exactly depressed, which is common for new double amputees, she was just no longer engaged in the world. She spent hours alone in her room, just imagining what her life would be like if she had turned left instead of right. Or took the bus instead of driving. Or had gotten her brakes looked at like the manual said. Eventually she was constructing elaborate fantasy lives, each rooted in just a single change to the circumstances of her past. Sometimes, her imaginings were so detailed that she would forget herself entirely, just wandering in her could-have-been selves. Until one day her fantasy was so believable that everyone else, the whole world, reality itself believed it as well.</p>

